invariant: INV-14
file: srv_flight.c
catches: srv_flight_test
reason: the second ClientHello of a retry leaves the signature scheme where the
  caller's selection had it. The tcp-nonblocking and QUIC drivers zero their
  selection before the second hello, so the scheme stays 0 there and
  every retried handshake that authenticates with a certificate fails at
  the Certificate with internal_error, which is how those two drivers
  first shipped. test/srv_resume_issue_tests.h runs the second hello over a
  zeroed selection and requires the first hello's scheme back.

--- old
    sel->sigalg = srv_select_sigalg(&h->t->cfg, ch->sigalgs);
    sel->need_retry = 0;
--- new
    sel->need_retry = 0;
